### Sample requests (IntelliJ HTTP client / VS Code REST Client). Run the app with the default `local` profile.

### 1) Create a checkout  -> 201 + Location + X-Correlation-Id + X-Trace-Id
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/checkouts
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-001
X-Client-Id: web-storefront

{
  "customerId": "cust-1001",
  "customerEmail": "john.doe@example.com",
  "currency": "USD",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-TSHIRT-M", "name": "T-Shirt (M)", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 19.99, "currency": "USD" },
    { "sku": "SKU-SOCKS",    "name": "Socks",       "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 5.00,  "currency": "USD" }
  ]
}

> {% client.global.set("checkoutId", response.body.checkoutId); %}

### 2) Get it
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/checkouts/{{checkoutId}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-002

### 3) Confirm -> calls payment-service via WebClient (watch both sides log the same traceId)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/checkouts/{{checkoutId}}/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-003

{ "paymentToken": "tok_visa_4242" }

### 4) Declined payment -> 422 CHK-422-002   (create a new checkout first)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/checkouts/{{checkoutId}}/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentToken": "tok_decline" }

### 5) Payment service down -> 2 retries, then 503 CHK-503-001
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/checkouts/{{checkoutId}}/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "paymentToken": "tok_unavailable" }

### 6) Validation error -> 400 CHK-400-001 with every field error
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/checkouts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "", "customerEmail": "nope", "currency": "usd", "items": [] }

### 7) Not found -> 404 CHK-404-001
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/checkouts/chk_00000000000000000000000000000000
